summary:
Extracted shared plugin-SDK primitives into framework/plugin/rs (PanelKit tree-item/selection helpers + PanelTreeBuilder, LocaleLabels trait + resolve_labels/is_de_locale + app_labels! macro + AppLabelsOverlayExt fluent builder, testkit module with meta/new_app/new_app_with_registry/paired_apps + assert_undo_redo_round_trip/assert_two_instances_converge/assert_ingest_idempotent, and a ResourceKindSpec + AppBuilder::resource_kind manifest primitive with a locally-defined OsMediaCapability enum). Added inline #[cfg(test)] coverage for every new primitive against a dummy DocumentApp — all pass.

De-apped the plugin SDK: moved the entire generate_mode and protocol_mode modules (protocol-domain rendering/op-builder code: render_question_field, render_generation_form_body, render_generation_preview_text, GenerationPlayState/GenerationOp CRUD, ProtocolBuilderConfig, add_step_op/add_block_op/etc., render_protocol_builder) out of framework/plugin/rs and into protocol/rs as two new modules (generation_forms, builder_kit), flattened via pub use at the protocol crate root. Removed the protocol dependency from framework/plugin/rs/Cargo.toml; added ui_wgpu as a dependency of protocol/rs (protocol did not previously depend on the UI layer).

Fixed call sites in protocol-plugin, procedural-plugin, and flow-plugin to import the moved symbols from `protocol` instead of `semio_framework_plugin`, adding the `protocol` Cargo dependency where needed. Also fixed procedural/2d/rs and procedural/3d/rs (domain crates that are direct compile dependencies of procedural-plugin and used the moved GenerationOp/GenerationPlayState symbols directly) — this was outside the ticket's nominal file-ownership list but required for the mandated `cargo check -p procedural-plugin` to pass; the fix is the identical mechanical import-source swap applied everywhere else.

While driving verification to green, fixed three pre-existing, unrelated compile breaks already present at HEAD in files I own this wave (not part of this ticket's substance, but blocking the required verification commands): a missing `loading: None` field in ~19 UiTreeItemNode/UiTreeSectionNode/UiTreeNode/UiSectionNode struct literals across procedural/plugin/rs and flow/plugin/rs (ui_wgpu added the field in a concurrent ticket; these two files hadn't caught up), and a missing `active_utility` argument to `render_generate_preview`/`preview_selection_json` in procedural/plugin/rs's Procedural3d generate-preview path. Also reconciled protocol/rs's new render_protocol_builder against a concurrent rename in ui_wgpu (UiComponentSceneNode.raster -> paint_2d, ProtocolListScene -> BlockListScene, ProtocolPaletteEntry -> BlockPaletteEntry) that landed mid-session.

Verification (see verification/ subfolder for full logs): cargo check -p semio-framework-plugin, -p protocol, -p protocol-plugin, -p procedural-plugin, -p flow-plugin all clean (zero errors, only pre-existing unrelated warnings). cargo test -p semio-framework-plugin: 76/76 passed. Also ran (beyond the mandated list) cargo test -p protocol (9/9), -p protocol-plugin (9/9), -p procedural-plugin (40/40), -p flow-plugin (16/16) — all green.

NOT expressible cleanly with existing primitives this wave (flagged for later waves):
- ResourceKindSpec/AppBuilder::resource_kind only threads through as a Rust-level field on the SDK's own `App` struct — `AppDefinition`/`PluginManifest` (framework-core, out of my ownership) have no `resource_kinds` field yet, so it does not round-trip through the JSON plugin-manifest wire format the way window_kinds/panel_tabs do. A later wave should add that field to AppDefinition and thread it through AppBuilder::build_definition.
- OsMediaCapability is duplicated (framework/plugin's new copy vs framework/product/os/core's original) because semio-framework-os already depends on semio-framework-plugin (a dependency in the other direction would cycle). A later wave should hoist one canonical definition into semio-framework-core (mirroring how OsMediaFormat already lives there) and have os/core re-export it.
- AppLabelsOverlay has no `app_label` field (removed from the struct by another concurrent session's edit before I started), so the Terminology region's fluent builder is an AppLabelsOverlayExt trait (orphan rules block inherent methods on a foreign type) covering only the fields that actually exist today: window_kind_label/panel_tab_label/mode_label/action_labels/utility_labels/example_labels/action_arg_label/dialog_labels/introduction_labels — no `.app_label()`.
- selection_ids() ships the majority 3-crate shape (`args["ids"]` only); ~5 other crates additionally fall back to a singular `id`/`nodeId` key and were left with their own wrapper for now (documented in the function's doc comment) rather than forcing a shape that doesn't fit every call site.
- forms/plugin/rs/lib.rs still imports ProtocolBuilderConfig/PROTOCOL_BUILDER_LABELS_EN/render_protocol_builder/BlockPaletteEntry from semio_framework_plugin (lines ~882-900) and will fail to compile until a follow-up swaps those three-plus imports to `protocol` — out of this wave's file-ownership list (not procedural/plugin or flow/plugin), so intentionally left untouched; cargo check -p forms-plugin was not in this ticket's mandated verification list.

MIGRATION GUIDE (paste verbatim into other agents' briefs):

## PanelKit (framework/plugin/rs, crate root `semio_framework_plugin::*`)
- `tree_item(id: impl Into<String>, label: impl Into<String>) -> UiTreeItemNode`
- `tree_item_desc(id: impl Into<String>, label: impl Into<String>, description: Option<String>) -> UiTreeItemNode`
- `tree_item_with_action(id: impl Into<String>, label: impl Into<String>, description: Option<String>, action: ActionDescriptor) -> UiTreeItemNode`
- `tree_item_with_action_draggable(id: impl Into<String>, label: impl Into<String>, description: Option<String>, action: ActionDescriptor, drag_data: &serde_json::Value) -> UiTreeItemNode` — drag_data is a JSON object; each entry becomes one MIME-type -> string drag-data pair (caller supplies the MIME key(s) explicitly; string values used verbatim, non-string values serialized).
- `selection_ids(args: Option<&serde_json::Value>) -> Vec<String>` — reads `args["ids"]` as an array of strings.
- `struct PanelTreeBuilder` — `PanelTreeBuilder::new(namespace: impl Into<String>) -> Self`, `.item_id(&self, kind: &str, id: &str) -> String`, `.section(id, label: Option<String>, default_open: bool, items: Vec<UiTreeItemNode>) -> Self`, `.section_or_placeholder(id, label, default_open, items, placeholder_label: impl Into<String>) -> Self`, `.selected(ids: Vec<String>) -> Self`, `.highlighted(ids: Vec<String>) -> Self`, `.selection_change(action: ActionDescriptor) -> Self`, `.drop_action(action: ActionDescriptor) -> Self`, `.build(self) -> UiNode`.

