## Terminology (framework/plugin/rs, crate root)
- `trait LocaleLabels: Sized + 'static { fn locale_labels_en() -> &'static Self; fn locale_labels_de() -> &'static Self; }`
- `fn is_de_locale(view_state: &ViewState) -> bool`
- `fn resolve_labels<L: LocaleLabels>(view_state: &ViewState) -> &'static L`
- `macro_rules! app_labels!` (macro_rules, `#[macro_export]`, invoke as `semio_framework_plugin::app_labels! { struct Name { field: &'static str = en: "...", de: "..."; ... } }`) — generates the struct, its `EN`/`DE` consts, and the `LocaleLabels` impl.
- `fn localized_label_map(is_de: bool, entries: &[(&str, &str, &str)]) -> HashMap<String, String>`
- `trait AppLabelsOverlayExt` (extension trait on `AppLabelsOverlay`): `.window_kind_label(id, label)`, `.panel_tab_label(id, label)`, `.mode_label(id, label)`, `.action_labels(HashMap<String,String>)`, `.utility_labels(...)`, `.example_labels(...)`, `.action_arg_label(key, label)`, `.dialog_labels(...)`, `.introduction_labels(...)` — all consuming/returning `Self` fluently.

Before (protocol/plugin/rs, pre-move):
```rust
struct ProtocolPlayLabels { mode_builder: &'static str, window_builder: &'static str, kind_arg: &'static str }
const PROTOCOL_PLAY_LABELS_EN: ProtocolPlayLabels = ProtocolPlayLabels { mode_builder: "Builder", window_builder: "Builder", kind_arg: "Kind" };
const PROTOCOL_PLAY_LABELS_DE: ProtocolPlayLabels = ProtocolPlayLabels { mode_builder: "Builder", window_builder: "Builder", kind_arg: "Art" };
fn protocol_play_labels(view_state: &ViewState) -> &'static ProtocolPlayLabels {
    if view_state.locale.as_deref().is_some_and(|l| l.starts_with("de")) { &PROTOCOL_PLAY_LABELS_DE } else { &PROTOCOL_PLAY_LABELS_EN }
}
// ... plus a hand-rolled semio_framework_plugin::AppLabelsOverlay { window_kind_labels: ..., mode_labels: ..., action_labels: protocol_play_action_labels(is_de), ... } struct literal in app_labels().
```
After:
```rust
use semio_framework_plugin::{app_labels, resolve_labels, is_de_locale, localized_label_map, AppLabelsOverlayExt};
app_labels! {
    struct ProtocolPlayLabels {
        mode_builder: &'static str = en: "Builder", de: "Builder";
        window_builder: &'static str = en: "Builder", de: "Builder";
        kind_arg: &'static str = en: "Kind", de: "Art";
    }
}
// in app_labels(&self, view_state):
let labels = resolve_labels::<ProtocolPlayLabels>(view_state);
let is_de = is_de_locale(view_state);
semio_framework_plugin::AppLabelsOverlay::default()
    .window_kind_label(PROTOCOL_PLAY_WINDOW_BUILDER, labels.window_builder)
    .mode_label("builder", labels.mode_builder)
    .action_labels(localized_label_map(is_de, &[("addStep", "Add Step", "Schritt hinzufuegen"), /* ... */]))
```

## Testkit (framework/plugin/rs::testkit, re-exported as `semio_framework_plugin::testkit`)
- `pub fn meta(actor: &str) -> ActionMeta`
- `pub fn new_app<A: DocumentApp + Default>() -> VcsDocumentApp<A>`
- `pub fn new_app_with_registry<A: DocumentApp + Default>(manifest: fn() -> App) -> VcsDocumentApp<A>`
- `pub fn paired_apps<A: DocumentApp + Default>(channel: &str) -> (VcsDocumentApp<A>, VcsDocumentApp<A>)`
- `pub fn assert_undo_redo_round_trip<A: DocumentApp, P: PartialEq + Debug>(app: &mut VcsDocumentApp<A>, action: &str, args: Option<&Value>, probe: impl Fn(&VcsDocumentApp<A>) -> P, before: P, after: P)`
- `pub fn assert_two_instances_converge<A: DocumentApp + Default, P: PartialEq + Debug>(channel: &str, action_a: (&str, Option<&Value>), action_b: (&str, Option<&Value>), probe: impl Fn(&VcsDocumentApp<A>) -> P)`
- `pub fn assert_ingest_idempotent<A: DocumentApp + Default, P: PartialEq + Debug>(action: &str, args: Option<&Value>, probe: impl Fn(&VcsDocumentApp<A>) -> P)`

Before (protocol/plugin/rs tests, pre-move):
```rust
fn meta(actor: &str) -> ActionMeta { ActionMeta { actor: actor.into(), instance_id: 1 } }
fn new_app() -> VcsDocumentApp<ProtocolPlayApp> { VcsDocumentApp::new(ProtocolPlayApp::default()) }
#[test]
fn two_instances_converge_disjoint_edits_via_backbone() {
    let mut instance_a = new_app(); let mut instance_b = new_app();
    let (backbone_a, backbone_b) = MemoryBackbone::pair("mem://protocol-convergence", "mem://protocol-convergence");
    instance_a.attach_backbone(Box::new(backbone_a)).expect("attach a");
    instance_b.attach_backbone(Box::new(backbone_b)).expect("attach b");
    instance_a.handle_action("addStep", None, &ViewState::default(), &meta("actor-a")).expect("a");
    instance_b.handle_action("addBlock", Some(&json!({"kind":"number"})), &ViewState::default(), &meta("actor-b")).expect("b");
    instance_a.handle_action("commitCheckpoint", None, &ViewState::default(), &meta("actor-a")).expect("pump a");
    instance_b.handle_action("commitCheckpoint", None, &ViewState::default(), &meta("actor-b")).expect("pump b");
    assert_eq!(instance_a.projection().unwrap().steps.len(), 2);
    assert_eq!(instance_b.projection().unwrap().steps.len(), 2);
}
```
After (control flow shared, only the app-specific action ids/probe stay local):
```rust
use semio_framework_plugin::testkit::{meta, assert_two_instances_converge};
#[test]
fn two_instances_converge_disjoint_edits_via_backbone() {
    assert_two_instances_converge::<ProtocolPlayApp, usize>(
        "mem://protocol-convergence",
        ("addStep", None),
        ("addBlock", Some(&json!({"kind":"number"}))),
        |app| app.projection().unwrap().steps.len(),
    );
}
```

## ResourceKindSpec (framework/plugin/rs, crate root)
- `struct ResourceKindSpec { id: String, name: String, source_format: String, component_kind: String, dimension: String, media_capability: OsMediaCapability }`
- `enum OsMediaCapability { MeshOnly, Brep }` (local to framework/plugin; structurally mirrors but does not share `semio_framework_os::OsMediaCapability` — see "not expressible" note above)
- `AppBuilder::resource_kind(mut self, spec: ResourceKindSpec) -> Self` — repeatable; collected into `App.resource_kinds: Vec<ResourceKindSpec>` (Rust-level only, not yet in the JSON manifest — see note above).

Before: no equivalent existed; apps/OS hardcoded resource-kind strings (e.g. `os_resource_media_capability` matching on `"3d.cad" | "3d.process" | ...`).
After (illustrative — AppDefinition wiring is a follow-up):
```rust
App::builder("procedural3d-play", "Procedural 3D")
    // ...
    .resource_kind(ResourceKindSpec {
        id: "3d.procedural".into(), name: "Procedural 3D".into(), source_format: "flow.fixture".into(),
        component_kind: "world3d".into(), dimension: "3d".into(), media_capability: OsMediaCapability::MeshOnly,
    })
```
